# Disable ALL line-ending conversion, repo-wide.
#
# This machine's git has core.autocrlf=true (system-level setting, not
# something this repo controls). That setting silently rewrites LF<->CRLF
# on every `git add`/`git checkout`, which just corrupted a byte-for-byte
# hash-based guardrail check: live_slc/guardrails.py and
# backtest/run_slc_backtest.py both hash-verify certain files (including
# utils/strategy_registry.py) against a frozen baseline, and `git checkout
# HEAD -- utils/strategy_registry.py` silently reintroduced CRLF into a
# file whose committed blob was LF, breaking the ALREADY-LIVE SLC paper-
# trading system's own safety gate with no actual content change. `-text`
# tells git to treat every path as binary for line-ending purposes, so
# add/commit/checkout never touch bytes, regardless of core.autocrlf.
* -text
